
# To Do List

A Java Swing task manager application that allows users to add and manage tasks in a scrollable GUI.

## Features

- Add new tasks in a scrollable task panel
- Delete tasks and manage individual checkbox state
- Uses a custom UI font and a compact task component layout
- Built with Swing and custom component composition

## Files

- `App.java` — application entry point and Swing EDT launcher
- `ToDoListGui.java` — main application window and task panel layout
- `TaskComponent.java` — individual task UI component with delete and checkbox behavior
- `ToDoList.java` — placeholder core class used by the app
- `CommonConstants.java` — shared UI size and style constants
- `resources/` — custom font resource used by the GUI

## Run

```powershell
cd "To Do List"
javac -d out src\*.java
java -cp out;resources App
```

> Note: The app loads a custom font from `resources/`. If you run from the terminal, include `resources` on the classpath or use an IDE that includes project resources automatically.
